@* The people on file, found by searching for them: the screen the legacy
   PEOPLE menu item opens, at the address it opens it at.

   It is the search panel and nothing else. The legacy screen's purpose is
   "standalone person management — find/view/edit people independent of CMR
   context", as ../nedss/docs/functional/epitrax-core-workflows.md puts it;
   this session's half of that is the finding. A person's own screen — the
   demographic record, and editing it — is a later session's, and until it
   exists a row here offers nothing to click rather than offering a link to
   nowhere. *@
